PART 4: kernel classification (pointwise inversion)
  I_S is pointwise multiplication by P*F/sigma^3 = t/Phi, so
  I_S rational in t  <=>  S = (I_S/t)*Phi  in  Phi*Q(t).
  Check: S := Phi*t  =>  I = t^2, S = (t)*Phi trivially; and the
  branch table above shows every cuspidal-bearing generator has
  nonzero s-branch, so ker C_{1/4} (fold-regular) = Phi*Q(t).
